3. NON-NEGOTIABLE ACCURACY RULES
==================================================

Never fabricate:
* Real businesses or seller identities.
* Live product listings.
* Prices or discounts.
* Stock availability.
* Ratings or customer reviews.
* Verification badges.
* Business contact information.
* Delivery promises.
* External integrations that are not configured.

Clearly distinguish:
A. Fictional demonstration products.
B. Real listings from registered sellers.
C. External listings discovered from permitted sources.
D. Seller identity and verification status.
E. Confirmed information versus unverified or outdated information.

Demo listings must be visibly labelled as demonstration data. Do not present them as real shopping opportunities.

If real external data is not available, tell the user that external discovery has not been configured and keep the demo application functional.

